                        ],
                        "form": "birred"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "20a87401-a07e-4169-8981-b73085c120b9",
                        "entry_id": "c291033d-13d3-31a7-829e-396d54193f6f",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "birred"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8beb34d6-4980-3bf0-b2dd-553254c6c5c4",
                        "entry_id": "c291033d-13d3-31a7-829e-396d54193f6f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To make a whirring noise; make a noise like that of revolving wheels, or of millstones at work."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "145f1a11-cee2-4515-8b0e-9ac0a47f2169",
                                "sense_id": "8beb34d6-4980-3bf0-b2dd-553254c6c5c4",
                                "text": "The muircock birrs at yer snell ha' door , An' fyles blawin' drift yer sheep will smore,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c64fd3b-21d5-4c0d-a3e6-4af7440cf81e",
                                "sense_id": "8beb34d6-4980-3bf0-b2dd-553254c6c5c4",
                                "text": "if it is ordained that ye must forget him, ye will banish him from your mind the mair easily that ye ken nae mair o' him than ye do o' the bird that birrs past ye in the wood—that it has a bonny feather in its tail.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2a204cf-5e82-449b-b271-585852a06046",
                                "sense_id": "8beb34d6-4980-3bf0-b2dd-553254c6c5c4",
                                "text": "The gudewife birrs wi ' the wheel a' day, Three threeds an' a thrum, Three threeds an' a thrum,"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9eb845e8-b8f8-3637-9fa3-41e796d8ab7b",
                        "entry_id": "c291033d-13d3-31a7-829e-396d54193f6f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To lurch or set to spinning."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d73cc83-3b5b-4e79-ac01-f51e50f845da",
                                "sense_id": "9eb845e8-b8f8-3637-9fa3-41e796d8ab7b",
                                "text": "His cowt grew reezy, its lang tail 'Twad swash, and lugs wad birr up, At length it cuist him, and did trail Him hame, by fit i'e stirrup,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e1ccc5f6-dcf4-4413-829a-b75610d51d10",
                                "sense_id": "9eb845e8-b8f8-3637-9fa3-41e796d8ab7b",
                                "text": "She's bow't i' the bacck, has a growth on her shouther, And hirples in daytime when steerin ' frae hame ; But nichtly birrs aff like a rocket o ' puother, And reels ' mang the staurs on a broomstick o ' fame ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d45cc36-7b1e-477f-9e40-d66a84415a3c",
                                "sense_id": "9eb845e8-b8f8-3637-9fa3-41e796d8ab7b",
                                "text": "When wark had ceased - fiel', Lads knitted, lassies trig an' clean, Did birr the spinnin' wheel;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "461e25ce-0f8b-48bc-a19f-49f5818d563f",
                                "sense_id": "9eb845e8-b8f8-3637-9fa3-41e796d8ab7b",
                                "text": "The swankies lap thro' mire and slike, Wow ! as their heads did birr: They yowph'd the ba' frae dike to dike, Wi ' unco' speed and virr,"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
